 that did not have the necessary items to clean the diaper changing station. The operation had been open at 6:00 am and at 10:00 am one classroom still did not have a sanitation solution to clean the changing table. The caregiver was unable to provide information on how the changing table was being cleaned this morning.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026311121","violation_type_title":"Diapering Procedures - Sanitizing Diaper Changing Area (26 TAC §746.3505(e))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241029-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3417-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241029","date":"2024-10-29","original_code":"746.3417(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-11-08","finding":"Children Handwashing After Toileting or Diapering: While watching video footage of another incident, I observed a caregiver changing an infants diaper and not washing the infants hands. I spoke to the office staff regarding what had been seen.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026230924","violation_type_title":"Children Handwashing After Toileting or Diapering (26 TAC §746.3417(3))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241029-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241029","date":"2024-10-29","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-11-08","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: Observed a child playing in the sink without a caregiver around to supervise. The caregiver in charge of the child did not know the child was missing. The class was outside while the child was inside the bathroom in the operation.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026431553","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241029-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407-12","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241029","date":"2024-10-29","original_code":"746.3407(12)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-11-08","finding":"Mark Cleaning Supplies, Toxic Materials; Keep Separate from Food and Inaccessible to Children: Observed a bottle of carpet and upolstry cleaner in an unlocked bathroom cabinet that children have access too. This was corrected when the cabinet was locked","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026471540","violation_type_title":"Mark Cleaning Supplies, Toxic Materials; Keep Separate from Food and Inaccessible to Children (26 TAC §746.3407(12))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241025","date":"2024-10-25","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":2,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905900131","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905900131","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-10-25","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241025-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2401-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241025","date":"2024-10-25","original_code":"746.2401(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-11-08","finding":"Basic Requirements for Infants - Holding and Comforting: It was observed in a video that an infant fell, started to cry and the caregiver did not comfort the infant.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026676126","violation_type_title":"Basic Requirements for Infants - Holding and Comforting (26 TAC §746.2401(3))","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241025-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1003-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20241025","date":"2024-10-25","original_code":"746.1003(3)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-11-08","finding":"Director Responsibilities - Employee Assignments: A caregiver was placed in an assignment that did not match their skills or abilities.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026672242","violation_type_title":"Director Responsibilities - Employee Assignments (26 TAC §746.1003(3))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240202","date":"2024-02-02","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905743281","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905743281","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-02-02","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240124","date":"2024-01-24","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":4,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905743280","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905743280","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-01-24","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240124-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240124","date":"2024-01-24","original_code":"746.3407","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-02-02","finding":"Maintenance of Building, Grounds and Equipment: The refrigerators and freezers had dried food and crumbs on the shelves and where food was stored.   The sinks and walls in the bathrooms and classrooms had food on them and were dirty.   There was a sink in another room that had a metal curtain rod on the sink. This was removed.   In the school age bathroom, there was not a toilet paper holder and the toilet paper was sitting on the trashcan.   The toilets were also dirty with yellow stains in the toilets.   There were two seats for the children in one room that were stained and had dirt build up on the chairs.   There was a broken table in the bathroom of the toddler room and a metal curtain rod on the sink in another bathroom. The table was removed from the bathroom.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026317966","violation_type_title":"Maintenance of Building, Grounds and Equipment (26 TAC §746.3407)","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240124-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240124","date":"2024-01-24","original_code":"746.3407(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Machine Wash Linens: Multiple infant sheets had dirt, stains and looks of dried wet spots on the sheets. The caregivers replaced the sheets with clean ones.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026438330","violation_type_title":"Machine Wash Linens (26 TAC §746.3407(3))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240124-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4135-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240124","date":"2024-01-24","original_code":"746.4135(b)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Children's Products- Annual Certification: The children product safety report had not been completed in the last two years. This was completed during the inspection.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026277563","violation_type_title":"Children's Products- Annual Certification (26 TAC §746.4135(b))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240124-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4409","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20240124","date":"2024-01-24","original_code":"746.4409","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Location of Toilets: In one classroom there was no toilet paper for the children to have indipendent use. I spoke to the director and caregiver about having toilet paper for the children.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026398323","violation_type_title":"Location of Toilets (26 TAC §746.4409)","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20230411","date":"2023-04-11","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905743279","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905743279","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-04-11","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20230331","date":"2023-03-31","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905743278","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905743278","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-03-31","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-95322-i20230329","date":"2023-03-29","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report (self-reported)","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":2,"open_count":0,"eviden